<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fulgencio Batista</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1901–1973</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fulgencio Batista was a Cuban army sergeant who rose to power after the revolution of 1933 and dominated Cuban politics for most of the next quarter-century. He was elected president in 1940 and seized power again in a coup in 1952. His corrupt dictatorship was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>'s revolutionaries, and he fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> on 1 January 1959.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fulgencio-batista.jpg" alt="Fulgencio Batista" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fulg%C3%AAncio_Batista_e_esposa,_1955_(cropped).tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
